 ## What is mapped
 
 Init and quit, hints, app metadata, events, windows and renderers, surfaces and pixel formats,
-gamepads, joysticks and haptics, keyboard and mouse, I/O streams, properties, filesystem paths,
-audio streams, and a mixer with tracks and WAV and MP3 input. Within each area, only the functions
-declared in `include/SDL3/s3_defs.h` and `include/SDL3_mixer/s3_mixer_defs.h` exist.
+gamepads, joysticks and haptics, HID devices, keyboard and mouse, I/O streams, properties,
+filesystem paths, audio streams, and a mixer with tracks and WAV and MP3 input. Within each area,
+only the functions declared in `include/SDL3/s3_defs.h` and `include/SDL3_mixer/s3_mixer_defs.h`
+exist.
 
 ## Known differences from SDL3
 
@@ -31,9 +32,14 @@ declared in `include/SDL3/s3_defs.h` and `include/SDL3_mixer/s3_mixer_defs.h` ex
 - On Switch, gamepads come from libnx instead of SDL2's joystick driver. Each of up to eight
   controllers is a gamepad only while it is connected, and its player index is the console's player
   number. SDL3's sideways mapping applies to a single Joy-Con. A controller that changes style,
-  such as a Joy-Con pair split in two, is removed and added again. Power levels are unknown, and
-  virtual joysticks, LEDs and sensors are not supported. `SDL_SendGamepadEffect` takes a libnx
-  `HidVibrationValue`, which plays on each of the controller's actuators until the next rumble call.
+  such as a Joy-Con pair split in two, is removed and added again. As a joystick it has the
+  gamepad's buttons up to the paddles and its six axes, the triggers spanning the joystick range.
+  Power levels are unknown, and virtual joysticks, LEDs and sensors are not supported.
+  `SDL_SendGamepadEffect` takes a libnx `HidVibrationValue`, which plays on each of the
+  controller's actuators until the next rumble call.
+- On Switch there are no HID devices to reach, so `SDL_hid_init` fails. Elsewhere the HID API is
+  SDL2's, and a device's bus type is always unknown.
+- Virtual joysticks have no sensors, so `SDL_SendJoystickVirtualSensorData` fails.
 - On Switch, `SDL_GetBasePath` is the folder of the running `.nro`, taken from the `sdmc:/` path the
   Homebrew Menu passes as `argv[0]`. Without such a path it is SDL2's answer, which on Switch is
   none.
